; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   362   \DESCRIPTION    A write access is performed on a pointer, which points to the memory address of the CSA frame. The
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   363                   memory address is derived from "Context->InitPCXI". The validity of "Context" is ensured by the
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   364                   caller. The content of "Context->InitPCXI" is also valid, because it is always initialized, before
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   365                   this pointer write access is performed. If "Context" is a task context, then its "InitPCXI" is
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   366                   initialized in Os_Hal_ContextInit and is re-initialized in Os_Hal_ContextReset and
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   367                   Os_Hal_ContextResetAndResume. If "Context" is an ISR/Hook context, then its "InitPCXI" is either
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   368                   initialized in Os_Hal_ContextInit or re-initialized in Os_Hal_Abort, when the ISR is killed.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   369                   As a result, whenever Os_Hal_ContextIntCleanupCSAs is called, "Context->InitPCXI" always contains
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   370                   a valid value. Thus, this write access is always performed on a valid pointer.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   371   \COUNTERMEASURE \N No measure is required, because its validity is ensured by code review.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   372  
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   373  \ID SBSW_OS_HAL_PWA_PCXI
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   374   \DESCRIPTION    A write access is performed on a pointer, which points to the memory address of the CSA frame. The
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   375                   memory address is derived from the PCXI register. Since Os_Hal_Svlcx is previously performed, the
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   376                   PCXI register always contains a valid value. Thus, this write access is always performed on a valid
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   377                   pointer.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   378   \COUNTERMEASURE \N No measure is required, because its validity is ensured by code review.
